# Working under `app/`

Until `app/AGENTS.md` exists, this rule plus `docs/STRUCTURE.md` (route layout)
are the authority on SEO, metadata, and indexing for every route.

Two things that are expensive to get wrong, stated here so they are never
missed:

1. **Default is `noindex`.** Portal routes (`app/(role)/owner/**`,
   `app/(role)/broker/**`) and anything behind auth must never be indexable.
   They contain private client and contact data. Public share pages are the
   exception and must be deliberate.
2. **Metadata must be server-rendered.** Crawlers read the HTML once and do
   not run React. Metadata set in a client component or `useEffect` is
   invisible to them.

Also: `app/` is routing only — fetch, compose, return. Business UI lives in
`features/`. Owner and broker trees never import from each other.
